---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import BrowserShot from "../components/BrowserShot.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const title = "Sidecar's companion dashboard — everything it kept, on your Mac";
const description =
  "The companion app's dashboard is a page on your own Mac that shows every chat, saved page, recording, and attachment Sidecar kept — read them, render Markdown and diagrams, reopen the original webpage, and delete anything. Nothing leaves your computer.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description} active="dashboard">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Companion dashboard</p>
      <h1>Everything Sidecar kept, in one place.</h1>
      <p>The companion app has a dashboard — a page that runs on your own Mac — where you can look through every chat, saved page, recording, and attachment, reopen the pages you asked about, and delete anything you don't want kept. Open it from the panel's <b>Settings → “Open admin page&nbsp;↗”</b>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:12px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <BrowserShot
        addr="127.0.0.1 · Sidecar dashboard"
        src="admin-dashboard.png"
        width={2360}
        height={2300}
        alt="The Sidecar dashboard: a sidebar of sections on the left, a table of conversations, and a live activity log with info, warning, and error lines."
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">What's inside</p><h2>Six views, one sidebar.</h2><p>Each section answers a different “what did it keep, and is everything working?”</p></div>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="uicard">
          <div class="ch">
            <span class="glyph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 11.5a8.4 8.4 0 0 1-12 7.6L3 20.5l1.4-5.4A8.4 8.4 0 1 1 21 11.5z"/></svg></span>
            <h3>Conversations</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Your chats with Sidecar — the ones saved on your Mac, plus any still running. Open one to read the whole thing back — more below.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="uicard">
          <div class="ch">
            <span class="glyph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><path d="M14 3v5h5"/></svg></span>
            <h3>Pages</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Text Sidecar saved from pages you discussed, so it can tell you what changed when you come back. “Forget this page” removes a page's saved text and remembered title.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="uicard">
          <div class="ch">
            <span class="glyph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 10v4M8 6v12M12 3v18M16 6v12M20 10v4"/></svg></span>
            <h3>Recordings</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Transcripts of what Sidecar heard when it listened to a tab, kept so re-watching doesn't mean listening again. Open one to read it in place.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="uicard">
          <div class="ch">
            <span class="glyph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="5" width="14" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M7 3h12a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v12"/><path d="M3 14l4-3 4 3"/></svg></span>
            <h3>Attachments</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Everything brought into your conversations — images and captured frames, plus attached files and quoted excerpts — with a link back to the exact message each came from.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="uicard">
          <div class="ch">
            <span class="glyph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 12h4l2 6 4-14 2 8h6"/></svg></span>
            <h3>Activity</h3>
          </div>
          <p>What the companion app is doing, as it happens — the same info, warning, and error lines you'd want when something isn't connecting. Filter to warnings and errors only.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="uicard">
          <div class="ch">
            <span class="glyph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="3" y="13" width="18" height="7" rx="2"/><path d="M7 7.5h.01M7 16.5h.01"/></svg></span>
            <h3>Environment</h3>
          </div>
          <p>The programs Sidecar relies on and whether they're installed on this computer — found here on your machine, nothing assumed. The place to look if Claude Code or Codex won't connect.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Reading a conversation</p><h2>Open a chat and read it back — your way.</h2></div>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="uicard">
          <div class="ch"><h3>Plain text or formatted</h3></div>
          <p>Every message shows as the exact text by default. Flip <b>“Render Markdown”</b> to read it formatted — headings, lists, tables, and code blocks — then flip it back to see the literal record. Your choice is remembered in this browser.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="uicard">
          <div class="ch"><h3>Diagrams as pictures</h3></div>
          <p>When an answer drew a diagram, the formatted view shows it as a picture instead of raw code — the same drawing you saw in the panel.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="uicard">
          <div class="ch"><h3>Reopen the original page</h3></div>
          <p>The page each message was about is a link — click it to reopen that webpage in a new tab and pick up where you were reading.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="uicard">
          <div class="ch"><h3>Download or delete</h3></div>
          <p>Save a conversation as a Markdown file to keep elsewhere, or delete it and everything saved with it — you get a few seconds to undo, then it's gone from your Mac for good.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Attachments</p><h2>Find that image or file again.</h2><p>Images and captured frames sit in a gallery; attached files and quoted excerpts sit in a list. Click any one to jump straight to the message it came from.</p></div>
      <BrowserShot
        addr="127.0.0.1 · Sidecar dashboard"
        src="admin-attachments.png"
        width={2360}
        height={2000}
        alt="The Attachments view: a gallery of image and video-frame thumbnails above a list of attached files and quoted excerpts, each labelled with the conversation it belongs to."
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Where it lives</p><h2>On your Mac, and only for you.</h2></div>
      <div class="outbound" style="margin-bottom:16px">
        The dashboard is served by the companion app on your own computer — at an address only your own Mac can reach (<span class="kbd">127.0.0.1</span>) — and is protected with a key kept on your Mac, so the websites you visit can't open it. It's a window onto what's already saved on your computer; none of your chats are sent anywhere. (Like the panel, the page loads its typefaces from Google Fonts — that one request carries nothing about you.) Deleting a conversation or forgetting a page removes it from your Mac.
      </div>
      <p class="kf-note">Open it any time from the panel's <b>Settings → “Open admin page&nbsp;↗”</b>. For the full picture of what's saved and what leaves your Mac, see <a href={`${base}privacy.html`}>Privacy&nbsp;&amp; control</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta-band">
        <h2>New to Sidecar?</h2>
        <p>Set up the extension and companion app in a few minutes, then everything above starts filling in.</p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${base}setup.html`}>Get set up</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${base}guide.html`}>Everyday controls</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
